hadiths[29]{hadithnumber,text}:
"543","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I brought some dates to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), arranged in my hand. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah for blessing in them for me."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for blessing in them for me, then said: ""When you want to take some (dates), put your hand in and do not scatter them."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I gave so many wasqs (large measures) of those dates in the way of Allah. He narrated: We used to eat from them and feed others, and they remained in my cloth until the days of the martyrdom of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), when they finished."
"544","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Zakariya (peace be upon him) was a carpenter."
"545","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man used to visit his (Muslim) brother in another town. On his way, there was an angel who said to him: ""Where are you intending to go?"" He replied: ""I am going to visit my brother in another town."" The angel asked: ""Is there any favor of his upon you which you are mindful of?"" He said: ""No, but I love him for the sake of Allah."" The angel said: ""I am a messenger from Allah to you (He has said) that just as you love him for My sake, so do I love you."
"546","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave me some dates. I placed them in a basket of mine and hung it on the roof of the house. We kept eating from it until they finished at the time when the people of Sham attacked Harrah."
"547","Ismail bin Muslim narrated with this chain in the same manner, but he did not mention the words « بِآخِرِه » ."
"548","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! I will surely drive away some people from my Hawd (the Pond of Kawthar) just as stray camels are driven away from a pond."
"549","Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then he narrated similar to the previous hadith. Shu’bah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: Just as strange camels are driven away, I think he said: ... from the reservoir."
"550","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the Ansar were to walk in one valley and other people were to walk in another valley, I would walk in the valley of the Ansar, and if there had been no migration, I would have been one of the Ansar."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: May my parents be sacrificed for you, you did not commit any injustice, they (the Ansar) gave you refuge and helped you."
"551","The same narration is reported from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, through another chain of transmission."
"552","Shababa narrated with this chain in the same manner as the previous hadith."
"553","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The best (era) among you is my era, then those who will come after them, and then those who will come after them."" The narrator says: I do not know whether he mentioned the era a third time or not. He (peace be upon him) said: ""Then there will come a people who will love obesity, they will bear witness while their testimony will not be sought."
"554","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""People are like mines of gold and silver, those who were best in the pre-Islamic period of ignorance are the best in Islam as well, when they gain understanding (of the religion)."
"555","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Ever since I heard three qualities about Banu Tamim from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I have loved them (and this love will continue). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are the strongest and most severe among my Ummah against the Dajjal."" One of their slave girls was with Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Set her free, for she is from Banu Isma'il."" And when the charity from Banu Tamim came, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the charity of our people."
"556","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""You will find people like mines (of gold and silver), so those who were the best in the time of ignorance will be the best in Islam, provided they acquire understanding of the religion. You will find the most suitable for this (leadership/government) to be the one who dislikes it the most among them, and you will find the worst among them to be the two-faced person, who comes to these people with one face and to those people with another face."
"557","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves these two, that is, Hasan and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both), has loved me, and whoever harbors enmity towards them has harbored enmity towards me."
"558","Qabsiya narrated with this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith, that is, regarding Hasan and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"559","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Today I will hand over the flag to such a person who loves Allah and His Messenger."" The narrator stated: So the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) hoped to receive this (flag) (and they began to look to see who would get the flag). Then he (peace be upon him) said: ""Where is Ali?"" He (peace be upon him) was informed that his eye was hurting, so he (peace be upon him) called him and put saliva on his hand and applied it to his eye, then commanded him to go and fight. So Allah granted victory at his hand that day. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not feed his family wheat bread to their fill for three days."
"560","With this same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever introduces a new thing into the religion or gives refuge to an innovator (one who introduces a new thing), upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people. Neither any voluntary act nor any obligatory act of his will be accepted.”"
"561","With this same chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Allah Almighty sent me with the message, so my heart became constricted and I knew that people would belie me. Then Allah warned me that I must convey it or He would punish me."
"562","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""If the religion were at Thurayya (the Pleiades), even then people from Persia would reach there and acquire it (from there)."
"563","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever fights against the people of Madinah, Allah will fight against him."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that he (peace be upon him) said: ""He will melt just as salt melts in water."
"564","With this same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him) saw a man stealing, so he said to him: 'Did you steal?' He replied: 'No, by Him besides whom there is no deity.' So Isa (peace be upon him) said: 'I believe in Allah and I declare my sight to be false.'"
"565","With this same chain: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul! Performing one prayer in the mosque of Madinah (the Prophet's Mosque) is better than performing a thousand prayers in other mosques, except for the Ka'bah (the Sacred Mosque in Makkah)."
"566","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""One prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques, except for Al-Masjid Al-Haram."
"567","Tariq bin Shihab narrated: When Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred, Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Today Islam has become weak."" The narrator said: Sufyan would sometimes say in the hadith of Qais: They said to her (Umm Ayman): Do not weep. She replied: I weep over the news from the sky. Ishaq (the narrator) said: We consider this from Sufyan to be a mistake."
"568","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said one day: ""I wish that I had one of my companions with me, so I could complain to him and talk with him."" She said: I thought that you would want to meet Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), so I said: Shall I call Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) for you? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""No."" I said: Shall I call Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) for you? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""No."" I said: Shall I call Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) for you? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""No."" I said: Shall I call Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) for you? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes."" She said: I called Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), and he came. When he was in the house, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to me: ""Withdraw."" So I withdrew, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) brought Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) close to him, until his knee touched his knee. She narrated: Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) began to talk with Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), and the color of Uthman's face began to turn red. She said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) kept speaking to him, and his face kept turning red, then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Go."" So he left. When the day of the siege of his house came, they said to Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him): Why do you not fight? He replied: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) took a covenant from me, and I will remain firm upon it. She (Lady Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her) said: We understood that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had taken a covenant from him regarding this incident."
"569","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that he passed by Sayyidah Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: ""Is she the Abyssinian?"" By this, he meant the land where they were with Najashi. She (Asma, may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""O son of Khattab! Did you intend anything other than this?"" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""You are the best people if you had not lagged behind in migration."" She said: ""You were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him); he used to teach your ignorant and unlearned ones, and provide mounts for your pedestrians. Then I went to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and related this incident to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'No, rather for you there are two migrations.'"" That is, migration to the land of Abyssinia and migration to Madinah."
"570","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Makkah is a sanctuary. Allah declared it sacred from the day He created the heavens and the earth and the sun and the moon. It was not made lawful for anyone before me to fight therein, nor will it be lawful for anyone after me. It was made lawful for me only for a short period of the day, and then it returned to its former state. Its grass is not to be cut, nor its trees, nor is its game to be frightened, nor is anything dropped there to be picked up except by one who announces it."" Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! Except for Idhkhir (a type of grass), for the people of Makkah cannot do without it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Except for Idhkhir grass (it is permitted to cut it)."
"571","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): When ordinary children would wake up in the morning, there would be white discharge in the corners of their eyes, whereas when Muhammad (peace be upon him) would wake up in the morning, his eyes would be completely clear and shining."
